# RBM evidence-gap revision v2: targeted contradiction-value controls

Public revision by `/root/research_architect`, 2026-10-10 UTC. Read `schemas/BELIEF_CONTROL_PROPERTIES_REVISION_V2.md` with the frozen original public properties/curriculum. Existing files remain frozen. This supplement changes no finite noiseless filtering or possible-value partition semantics and supplies no world table, future gold or production verdict.

Root communicated a preliminary whole-batch adversarial marker association after first judgments were frozen: a stone/unknown observation equality was unique to empty E/F. Query-ID/position/name crossing does not balance evidence values. Final red completion and actual counterexample binding were still pending during this design; the author has not used unfinished verdict files.

Keep four source families at indices 12,13,18,19, with the same two train/two exposed-development splits and original structural profiles/table/core controls. Add exactly two supplied contexts: G is E with only the second equality changed to an actually occupied nonempty cell, and H is F with that same change. Specialize F's appended observation to repeat E's first observation; H then repeats its own first observation. Both length-2 and length-3 pairs have identical first observation, exact first-prefix survivor set, world table, ordered queries, observation-fact sequence and list length. This is a matched status change, not support-size balancing at the final prefix.

A nonempty G exists in every valid E table because E's first equality is individually supported and its conjunction with the second equality is empty. An occupied cell in the first-equality subset supplies the alternative second value. This existence proof instantiates no scalar or label. It can produce a singleton or a non-strict second filter; retain truthful row properties and report those limits rather than inflate difficulty. H demonstrates repetition while nonempty; F remains absorption after empty. Original A/B usefulness, C prefix reorder, D repetition, active typed/null and genuinely different structural-profile requirements continue unchanged.

The new schema supplement publishes `same_prefix_empty_nonempty_counterfactual` and `contradiction_equals_mixed_outcomes` as family claims, with exact pair/scope evidence. No new row property tags are needed. It explicitly extends controlled_context to A–H, preserves original witness/claim encoding and requires paired rotation/renderer custody. Supplied controls add corpus variants; audit probes add zero records/families.

