All counts are prospective. Eight contexts remain descendants of four world tables. Planned nonempty frequency is 6/8=75%; length-2 contexts are 4/5 nonempty and length-3 contexts are 2/3 nonempty. A majority status baseline therefore remains material. Future exact entailed/useful/type/count histograms are unknown until independently derived.

The acceptance gate is actual mixed outcomes for E/G and F/H in every family/length/split, including typed equality and exact first-prefix support matches; the original frozen marker rule must make documented errors. Publish all scalar-anywhere and scalar-position/fact-role outcome histograms, coarse world/list/first-prefix buckets, actual query triple histograms, full targets and complete-task baseline errors. Annotation schedule success alone is insufficient. A different perfect input shortcut is a new finding, not a reason to retrospectively weaken the design.

This controls one concrete marker association. It does not promise every scalar/position bucket is mixed; positive-only literals and finite table/conjunction lookup can persist. Broader scalar balancing would require more supported empty/positive cells and independently audited contexts. Residual class imbalance, cyclic schedule patterns, shared motifs and exposed dev remain disclosed. There is no efficacy or sealed generalization evidence.

G/H are honest filtering/repetition controls, sometimes Level 2. Measure actual world/fact/observation counts, strict-filter count, final distinct payload count and essential constraints; original A's two necessary constraints and active typed partitions support Level 3 components. Extra contexts and views alone do not increase difficulty or mechanism independence.

Generation, formal solver, frozen first expert/red judgments and final adjudication are later separate executions. This author's original-design and later-adjudicator roles and shared-model risk must be disclosed. Root must confirm completed final red evidence before any v1 adjudication; future v2 likewise needs fresh completed exact-hash evidence. Interface/probe provenance reconciliation is a separate machine-evidence issue, not a new correctness proof.
